  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'The Statue of Zoroaster is a modern artistic representation of Zoroaster
    (Zarathustra), the ancient Iranian prophet traditionally associated with the
    foundation of Zoroastrianism. Unlike many Achaemenid artifacts, there is no securely
    identified ancient statue of Zoroaster from the Achaemenid period. Zoroastrianism
    had a major influence on Iranian religious and cultural traditions, and its ideas
    continued to shape Persian civilization for centuries.

    Zoroaster is commonly
    depicted wearing traditional Iranian clothing and holding or standing near a
    sacred fire, an important symbol in Zoroastrian religious tradition. His teachings
    emphasized the importance of truth, righteousness, good thoughts, good words,
    and good deeds. Modern representations of Zoroaster are therefore better understood
    as cultural or religious interpretations rather than historically verified portraits
    of what he actually looked like.'
